<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bank of Brazil</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Bank of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a> was founded in 1808 by the Portuguese prince regent João after the royal court moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-de-janeiro">Rio de Janeiro</a>. It was reorganised several times during the nineteenth century. It became an important financial institution of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazilian-empire">Brazilian Empire</a>, involved in issuing currency and financing the state.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bank-of-brazil.jpg" alt="Bank of Brazil" width="315" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alex Pereira · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:BBsedeI-a.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
